00:19:27,161 --> 00:19:32,220
rather than try to just manhandle it, just force it up and down with the strength of their bodies.

251
00:19:32,221 --> 00:19:45,840
Sailors used large cargo nets made of rope to lift all types of goods onto the ships,

252
00:19:45,841 --> 00:19:49,697
but one item in particular made up the bulk of the cargo.

253
00:19:49,698 --> 00:19:52,200
For both safety of the goods and ease

254
00:19:52,201 --> 00:19:58,880
of movement, the simple cask was the 19th century equivalent of the modern metal container.

255
00:19:58,881 --> 00:19:59,581
It was

256
00:19:59,582 --> 00:20:01,348
used to contain all different types of objects.

257
00:20:01,349 --> 00:20:03,160
It could contain wine, water, and whiskey,

258
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:07,480
the things that we normally think of being carried in casts, but it could also contain nails,

259
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:11,580
apples, china packed in sawdust, toys, parts of other casts,

