00:25:11,860 --> 00:25:18,500
Each can carry 200 containers, which means this facility loads and unloads up to 2,000 containers every week.

327
00:25:20,620 --> 00:25:27,760
Steel containers may be new, but freight has been loaded on train cars almost since the first trains rolled down the tracks.

328
00:25:28,680 --> 00:25:38,320
Right around 1830, 1831, you see the beginnings of freight cars being developed and experiments beginning on different types.

329
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:45,580
But early rail workers faced the same problem that plagued other forms of transportation, back-breaking labor.

330
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:52,340
One of the disadvantages is that the surface that goods were loaded on was much higher than the ground.

331
00:25:52,341 --> 00:26:02,140
And at the very beginning, it basically was manpower that struggled, whether it be hogsheads or crates or whatever, off a flat car down to the ground.

332
00:26:02,980 --> 00:26:06,920
Fortunately for early loading dock workers, the struggle would soon end.

333
00:26:06,921 --> 00:26:14,400
About 1845, leading up to 1850, in the big city passenger depots, we see the creation of the platform.

334
00:26:14,820 --> 00:26:17,260
This was used not only for people, but also for freight.

335
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:23,540
The platform was a structure meant to elevate a flat surface at the same level as the door of a boxcar,

336
00:26:23,660 --> 00:26:25,360
or a passenger car, or a freight car.

337
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:31,760
So it's easy then, instead of hefting materials out of the side of a boxcar down to the ground,

338
00:26:31,761 --> 00:26:35,720
to unload them on this platform, at the end of which was a long ramp,

339
00:26:36,100 --> 00:26:39,800
which a wheeled vehicle like a hand truck or a wagon could easily negotiate.

340
00:26:40,740 --> 00:26:46,900
Where platforms weren't available, workers used push carts for boxes and trunks small enough to be moved by hand.

341
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:54,220
Here are some early examples of baggage parts and the freight equipment that was loaded upon them.

342
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:56,660
These were usually taken outside the station.

343
00:26:56,661 --> 00:27:02,640
They were loaded from vehicles, whether it be wagon or truck, placed upon the car here,

344
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:07,620
which got them to a reasonable height so they could be transloaded into the door of the baggage car.

345
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:14,340
But in time, the railroad would be used to carry a far heavier burden.

346
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:20,760
The American Civil War was one of the first major conflicts to rely heavily on modern transportation.

347
00:27:20,761 --> 00:27:28,080
new loading dock technology would forever change both railroads and the face of war

